  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Rotary Parallel keeps its cut over the picked faces. The kernel plans the raster on the full model, as before. Then it keeps each cut point where the line from the axis through the ball centre meets a picked facet. The radial relink builds the links between the kept pieces.\n- The axis fit, the gouge laws and the verify still read the full model.\n- Rotary Parallel refuses, by name, a selection that it cannot use:\n  - a pick that is not a face;\n  - picks on two models;\n  - a face that does not look away from the axis (an end face, a bore wall);\n  - picks that form separate groups;\n  - picks that no pass lies over.\n- Rotary Contour and Rotary Offset refuse a face selection by name. They do not cut the full model silently. Face containment for these two kinds is not in this PR: #2851 (Rotary Contour) and #2852 (Rotary Offset) hold that work.\n- The generation stamp of a rotary operation with a selection gets a version mark. A path that was cached under the old reading becomes stale.\n- An operation with no selection (source `Entity` or `Stock`) generates as before.\n\nNew files:\n\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary_pick.rs`: the clip, `faces_outward`, `groups`.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/rotary_picks.rs`: the picks read from the world, and the refusals.\n- `crates/app/tests/rotary_face_selection.rs`: the pins.\n- `docs/decisions/2848-rotary-face-selection.md`: the decision record.\n\n## Cause\n\n`material_of` reads a selection as the full facets of the picked models. The rotary arms of `run_job` gave those facets to the kernels. No code read which faces were picked, and no code refused the selection.\n\n## Scope against the issue's \"Done means\"\n\n| Item | State |\n|---|---|\n| Rotary Parallel accepts `SrcRef::Selection` | done |\n| Rotary Contour, Rotary Offset accept `SrcRef::Selection` | not done: they refuse by name; #2851, #2852 |\n| Toolpath stays in the picked faces | done for Rotary Parallel |\n| Axis fit uses the full model | done, pinned |\n| Stock simulation reads only the generated toolpath | no change necessary: the simulation reads the stored path |\n| UI enables face selection for rotary operations | no change necessary: `SetOperationGeometry` has one door for all kinds (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) |\n| Unusable selections refuse with a clear message | done for all three kinds |\n| Full-model operation is the same | done: the `None` path is the old code |\n| Tests | done |\n\nThe maintainer's triage comment names the defect: the operation ignores the selection without a message. This PR removes that for all three kinds. If the maintainer wants the issue open until #2851 and #2852 merge, change `Fixes` to `Refs`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (`crates/app/tests/rotary_face_selection.rs`), all red on `upstream/main` 326c938b1:\n\n- `rotary_parallel_keeps_its_cut_over_the_picked_faces` - red before: \"a cut at station -16 is off the picked neck (2..16)\".\n- `rotary_parallel_keeps_to_a_sector_and_still_turns_about_the_whole_models_axis`.\n- `rotary_parallel_reads_a_welded_wall_pick_as_its_strips` - red before: \"a cut at station -16.204 is off the picked patch\".\n- `rotary_parallel_refuses_a_selection_it_cannot_use_by_name` - red before: \"the selection must be refused, not cut\".\n- `rotary_contour_and_offset_refuse_a_face_selection_by_name` - red before: \"the selection must be refused, not cut\".\n\nUnit tests (`multiaxis::rotary_pick::tests`): the clip, `faces_outward`, `groups`.\n\nMutations (each was put in, the pins ran, the fix was put back):\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| The two rotary arms of `generate.rs` as before the fix | 5 of 5 pins red |\n| The kernel clip off (`rotary_parallel_over` ignores the picks) | 3 keep pins red |\n| A chain pick read as \"no facets\" (no \"is not a face\" refusal) | refusal pin red |\n| The `faces_outward` guard off | refusal pin red |\n| The `groups` guard off | refusal pin red |\n\nA file-level restore of `generate.rs` from `upstream/main` does not compile with the new job field. The arm-level mutation replaced it.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 294 steps, 0 failed, wall 25.2 min. `upstream/main` moved to 5fdbed9bd during the work, so the gate selected the suites of those new commits too. The branch base is 326c938b1; the new commits do not touch `crates/app/src/operation` or `crates/motion/src/multiaxis`.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nThe gate ran with the compile cache off (`CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`, no `RUSTC_WRAPPER`). The sccache server of this machine did not answer.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The stamp version mark has no pin. A stamp under the old law cannot be made in a test.\n- A WCS yaw (#760) with a face selection. The picks are facet indices, so they follow the turned material, but no test runs that pair.\n- A part alignment (#326) with a face selection.\n- The ramped infeed (`entry_ramp`) on clipped passes. The relink code is not changed, and its ramps are proved against the full part.\n- A large sculpted pick (many thousands of facets): the time of the shadow test was not measured.\n- No GUI run. No screenshot: the PR changes no UI code.\n- The MCP `set_operation_geometry` door does not say the rotary refusals at the pick. Generation says them.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nOpen PRs #2836, #2833, #2831, #2822, #2716, #2714 and #2678 change `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` (and some change `job.rs` or `mod.rs`). They touch the same file, different arms of `run_job`. No open PR changes the rotary arms or `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Rotary Parallel keeps its passes to the picked faces; Rotary Contour and Rotary Offset refuse a face selection by name and no longer cut the full model silently (#2848).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2848\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
